than anyone in this room had been allowed to see. Blackwell had stood at =
this rail on a hundred nights in the empty lab, and every time, he felt the=
 cold breath of the engine rising from the pit.]
What ascended through the =
facility's foundation, and protruded into this observation chamber was a =
